    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0324" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/178: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                    France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-05T19:00:00-04:00">August 5, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–449. Your despatch no. 1433 of February 9, 1938,<anchor n="86" xml:id="d304-f1"
                    /> Antonio Fernandez and wife. Information received by Vice Consul Fisher from
                    Palma de Mallorca and in letters from Antonio Fernandez to his brother in New
                    York indicate that he has been hospitalized suffering from chronic nervous
                    ailment aggravated by continued imprisonment. In view of assurances of favorable
                    consideration of case given in General Jordana’s letter of February 5, 1938 and
                    the long time which has since elapsed, you are requested again to bring this
                    case informally to the attention of General Jordana and to express the hope that
                    in view of Fernandez’ physical condition it may be possible to permit his
                    release and return to the United States together with his wife.<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d304-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d304-f1" n="86" xml:id="d304-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see the Ambassador’s telegram No. 445, February 8, 7 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg271">p. 271</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f2" n="87" xml:id="d304-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram No. 509, August 6, 1 p.m., the Ambassador reported that a letter had
                    gone that day to General Jordana (352.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/177).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
